  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "Tied through six innings, then McNeil broke it open in the seventh.",
    "what_this_means": "This team doesn't need to lead early to win. They needed one inning to matter more than the other, and they got it. The offense stalled for five innings. Four runners in scoring position across the second and third without converting a single one. Arizona tied it at two in the sixth. Then the seventh arrived, and the game changed shape. McNeil's single was the moment, but it came with runners already in motion. The lineup had finally strung together something. That's the difference between this game and the empty nights: they didn't fold when they were matched. They waited for their moment and took it when it came. This is not a team that dominates. They survive tied games and break them late.",
    "what_to_watch": "Kohl Drake threw a 4.38 ERA into a lineup that has done something before. Tonight he faces a team that just proved it doesn't have to score early to finish a game.",
